y S. Thiede | President, CEO & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $2.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 9K people. Revenue per employee of $399K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $10K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $671 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Everus Construction Group, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $3.9B market cap on $3.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +31% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 21% against a 11% cost of capital \u2014 a 11-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, and 12% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $90M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.78\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 12\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.13454821131710237},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Industrials peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 21% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 26% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Growing faster than most Industrials peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"ECG Q3 Earnings Call Highlights Record Backlog and Raised Outlook","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024404/ecg-q3-earnings-call-highlights-record-backlog-and-raised-outlook?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog_plus%7Cearnings_call_takeaways-3024404","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793887200.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Everus Construction Group Inc (ECG) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Record Backlog and ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/